{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The caliper feels useful now because it would help me measure my screws and washers and work out which sizes fit together.",
    "The epoxy fits my interest in practical repairs, although I would wait for a specific bonding job before buying it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The electrical connectors assume I have a wiring or battery-cable project, which my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "The imperial nuts do not match my recent metric screw assortment, and four rolls of sealing tape would require a sealing job I do not currently have.",
    "The COVID test and temperature gun do not help with the fastening, measuring, or storage tasks I am interested in right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in workshop supplies seems to have been treated as interest in almost any repair or electrical supply.",
    "Buying hardware assortments seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest other large kits, even when they serve unrelated tasks."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The useful connection is how an item helps me use my existing screws, washers, and hooks; the caliper makes that connection directly.",
    "Exact sizes and compatibility matter: metric screws do not give me a reason to buy imperial nuts.",
    "I rarely buy without a relevant task, so even a plausible repair supply like epoxy can be something I would postpone."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my practical hardware interests but stretched them into unrelated workshop projects instead of focusing on what helps me use my current supplies."
}"}
